    {
      "text": "for the elect’s sake those days shall be shortened, Matt. 24:22 (Mark 13:20). they shall deceive the very elect, Matt. 24:24 (Mark 13:22; JS—M 1:22). they shall gather together his elect, Matt. 24:31 (24:22; JS—M 1:27). Ye have not chosen me, but I have chosen you, John 15:16. heirs of God, and joint-heirs with Christ, Rom. 8:17. Israelites; to whom pertaineth the adoption, Rom. 9:4. purpose of God according to election might stand, Rom. 9:11. remnant according to the election of grace, Rom. 11:5. that we might receive the adoption of sons, Gal. 4:5. chosen us in him before the foundation of the world, Eph. 1:4. Put on therefore, as the elect of God, Col. 3:12. Knowing, brethren beloved, your election of God, 1 Thes. 1:4. God hath from the beginning chosen you to salvation, 2 Thes. 2:13. I charge thee before God … and the elect angels, 1 Tim. 5:21. endure all things for the elect’s sakes, 2 Tim. 2:10. according to the faith of God’s elect, Titus 1:1. Elect according to the foreknowledge of God the Father, 1 Pet. 1:2. ye are a chosen generation, a royal priesthood, 1 Pet. 2:9. give diligence to make your calling and election sure, 2 Pet. 1:10. elder unto the elect lady, 2 Jn. 1:1.",
